Gaokao-Bench Changelog
======================

Versioning
----------
- Engine versions track the harness, scorer, CLI, packaging, and release tools.
- Dataset versions track questions, answers, points, assets, and manifest policy.
- A published result must record both versions plus the dataset and protocol hashes.

2026-11-18
----------

Dataset 0.1.0

- Assemble the first cumulative package: 2025 全国 I / 全国 II / 北京 / 上海 /
  天津 plus 2026 全国 I, closing at 119 questions / 900 points, with 88
  questions / 426 points scored deterministically and a 31-question,
  474-point subjective catalog. The single primary metric remains
  `score.weighted_points = earned / 426`.
- Introduce the mixed evidence contract `mixed_source_audit_v1`. It keeps the
  `strict_dual_source_v4` floor untouched and instead records the tier each
  question actually reaches in `source_audit.jsonl#evidence_level`, so a
  package can ship strong and thin papers side by side without claiming one
  quality level for both. Every question still needs hash-checked frozen
  evidence, and a tier that disagrees with its own group counts fails
  validation.
- 2026 全国 I keeps full `strict_dual_source_v4` evidence: 19/19 questions with
  nine independent stem groups and six independent joint groups.
- The five 2025 papers ship at their measured tiers: 73 questions at
  `stem_corroborated_v1` and 27 at `single_source_v1`. They do not reach
  `dual_source_v2` because no second publisher group carries both the stem and a
  verifiable answer for the same question; that is a measured gap, not an
  assertion, and `reports/audit-2025/` records the per-question group matrix.
- Rebind 天津 to the archived PDF (SHA-256 `70f4bb30...`) instead of the
  recalled reconstruction that `0.1.0-alpha.6.1` cited: crops are re-rendered
  from the PDF's own block geometry, page numbers and bounding boxes are
  refreshed, and the paper and source rows record the corrected digest.
- Re-read 天津's stems and distractor text from that PDF. Five multiple-choice
  questions carried distractor text the paper does not print — Q01's A/B/C,
  Q04's A, Q05's C/D, Q06's A/B/D and Q08's C — and seven stems were
  paraphrases of the printed wording. Every recorded answer was re-mapped through the option text
  the old package marked correct; no answer letter changed, because in each case
  the correct option survived the corruption. All 17 diffs, seven stems and
  ten option lines, are in `reports/audit-2025/tj-corrections.json`.
- Fix three release-tool defects found while assembling the package: the release
  gate referenced `checks` before assignment, the quality contract rejected any
  level other than `strict_dual_source_v4`, and the source audit hardcoded the
  strict policy floor for every package.
- Add `scripts/build_0_1_0.py` (mixed-package builder), `scripts/audit_2025_sources.py`
  (structural coverage), `scripts/measure_2025_question_sources.py`
  (per-question publisher groups), and `scripts/check_2025_stem_equivalence.py`
  (stem-vs-PDF agreement). Rebuilding is deterministic from the frozen caches.
- `owner_signoff` is still `pending`; the package is a release candidate, not a
  signed release.

2026-11-16
----------

Dataset 0.1.0-alpha.2026-n1.5.1

- Close the signed 2026 National Paper I package. Three independent audits, A,
  B and C, pass all 19 questions with no issues; the project owner then signs
  the full paper and every scored answer, point row, and figure asset. The
  package records `audited_passed` and does not claim external human reviewers.
- Keep the content identical to `0.1.0-alpha.2026-n1.5`; only review and owner
  attestation metadata changed. Final manifest SHA-256 is
  `f88f294c1b20c676121529e0b764ae2401bb1193e309e446e656748247552c2b`.
- Record 14 scored objective questions / 73 points plus a five-question,
  77-point subjective catalog. The full paper is 19 questions / 150 points.
  The scored slice has zero image-required questions; the full-paper catalog
  has one figure-bearing subjective question, so this release does not measure
  vision capability.
- Preserve the strengthened source gate for all 19 questions: nine independent
  stem groups, six independent joint stem+answer groups, 19/19 stem dual-source
  coverage, 19/19 joint answer dual-source coverage, and 138 frozen evidence
  pages. Future questions must meet the same gate before owner acceptance.
- Ship the same evidence in the Hugging Face public projection: `source_audit.jsonl`,
  `source_pages.jsonl`, all 138 frozen source pages, the pinned source specs, and
  the independent A/B/C audit reports. The public package now has 179 payload
  files and validates the dual-source gate directly; its manifest SHA-256 is
  `63fc423a866646dce96c394bb79b11ee3480e81e43a48e9165cba532b45c849a`.
- Make public-package validation run the dual-source gate, resolve source ledgers
  from `audit/`, preserve subjective reference answers needed by that gate, and
  verify the public projection's own content lineage. Pinned repository specs
  remain required when available but do not block data-only consumers.
- Fix the Hugging Face uploader so the default commit message follows the
  resolved dataset version instead of the repository default `0.0.4`.
- Allow the passing full-data candidate ZIP to include frozen source-page PDFs
  under `data/<version>/source_pages/`; the code-only artifact continues to
  reject all PDFs, images, question data, and evidence.
- Let the acceptance dashboard verify a materialised package's own
  `owner_signoff.json`, `review_protocol.json`, review events and declared input
  hashes when no separate mutable review packet exists.
- Allow pinned source specs to retain the audited source-version pin only for an
  owner-attested, content-unchanged metadata patch. Unrelated version drift
  remains a validation error.
- Add the version-bound release policy and public-contamination disclosure for
  `retrospective_public_2026`: freshness claims are disabled, public rights are
  CC BY 4.0 with attribution, and `public-code` remains a clean-revision,
  allowlisted code/documentation release.

